<title>CHINA: TEXWINCA YEARLY PROFIT RISES 62 PERCENT.</title>
<headline>TEXWINCA YEARLY PROFIT RISES 62 PERCENT.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-08-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended March 31</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	   40.8     vs 27.1</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)    5.0	vs 4.0</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	  nil	vs nil</p>
<p>    Net			    245.79   vs 151.72</p>
<p>    Turnover		     1,805.10 vs 1,048.29</p>
<p>    Company name		 Texwinca Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		  September 18-25</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	   October 23</p>
<p>NOTE - Texwinca is a fabric dyeing and knitting group.</p>
<p>The company proposes that each of the existing shares of HK$0.10 each be subdivided into two shares of HK$0.05 each to improve the market liquidity of the shares.</p>
<p>Total dividend for the year is eight H.K. cents (including interim dividend of three cents) vs 6.5 cents.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong News Room (852) 2843 6368</p>
</text>
